{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-vzin-a6pi-qvqt-4lsa","published":"2026-11-11T16:43:39Z","modified":"2026-11-23T17:45:05.064227621Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-116269"],"summary":"MIME::Field::ParamVal versions before 5.521 for Perl turn an RFC 2231 filename with a hyphenated language tag into an…","details":"MIME::Field::ParamVal versions before 5.521 for Perl turn an RFC 2231 filename with a hyphenated language tag into an empty recommended filename.\n\nA parameter such as filename*=utf-8'en-US'payload.exe is converted to an encoded word with the language tag appended to the charset. The decoder strips the language suffix only when it is a single word, so it cannot resolve the charset UTF-8*EN-US and returns an empty string. The recommended_filename() method returns that empty string rather than falling back to the name parameter.\n\nOther mail readers return payload.exe. A remote sender can get an attachment past a policy that checks file extensions on the recommended filename.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"perl-mime-tools","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/perl-mime-tools"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"5.517-r0"}]}],"versions":["5.517-r0","5.517-r1"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-vzin-a6pi-qvqt-4lsa.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://scout.docker.com/v/DHI-vzin-a6pi-qvqt-4lsa"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-116269"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://security.alpinelinux.org/vuln/CVE-2026-116269"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://alas.aws.amazon.com/AL2/ALAS-2026-4095.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116273"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116271"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116270"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116269"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116268"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116267"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://alas.aws.amazon.com/AL2023/ALAS-2026-3425.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116272"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116265"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116264"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-116269"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-116269"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://people.ubuntu.com/~ubuntu-security/cve/CVE-2026-116269"}],"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N"}]}